  "contributors": "Christopher Daniel Pang supplied the PAL point and horizon picture, the marker/payload question and the RPL/BLA direction. Hearthline derived these board formulations, constants and proofs in his independent constructive program.",
  "formal_scope": "Existence of a single threshold representing the truth of every cutoff, active tag or zero, actual least cutoff five for the modified size-256 frame, survivor factor classification, unordered uniqueness and exact triangle count. The four separately fixed finite statements were independently compared.",
  "paper_scope": "Growth of the least genuine cutoff gives the supremum of nontrivial zero real parts after taking max with one half. Lowering the root cutoff by the cube root of five eighths of the integer hyperbola count cancels the prime-square mean. Both signs exceed the one-seventieth bit allowance infinitely often on fourth powers. Eventual overflow at most two fifteenths of a bit per n*sqrt(n) unit is equivalent to RH, and this universal bound is outstanding.",
  "self_review": {
    "level": "author self-review",
    "orientation": "Use unordered prime products; each off-diagonal label is one distance and each square is counted once. The exact number of ordered-offset levels is cubic.",
    "constants": "Area integral 4/3 on ordered pairs, halved off the diagonal; each label has two orientations and asymptotic log weight 2*log(sqrt(n)). Total extra leading cost 16/3 times C^3, matched against 10/3.",
    "off_line_cases": "The least-cut equivalence at exponent a uses only the declared zero-free half-plane in the direction that pays the board. The compulsory swings of the calibrated board use one actual simple zero with no exclusion of other zeros.",
    "sampling": "The additional short-interval prime count makes the chord affine up to little-o at scale n^(3/2). Positivity of interpolation weights transfers either finite normalized endpoint bound even without a uniform two-sided error for the endpoints.",
    "control_ranges": "Complete critical margins are computed at ten selected roots through 80; larger roots through 10000 have only the new pair/dial cost. These finite data play no role in proving infinite recurrence."
  },
